WEBVTT

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:10.990
This story is a work of fiction. All persons and organizations are imagined. 
The kabaddi and game rules which appear in this anime are drawn from the original work.

00:00:07.130 --> 00:00:09.980
<i>How many points did he just take from us?</i>

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:18.840
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:13.780
<i>This is no time to worry about that!</i>

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:16.040
<i>I have to look for an opening and strike!</i>

00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:21.000
<i>If I can stop him for even a split second,
 then, just like always, he'll...</i>

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:24.040
Kabaddi!

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:25.030
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:27.750
<b>Date</b>

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:27.750
<b>Misumi</b>

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:27.750
Damn it!

00:00:28.190 --> 00:00:29.660
Okay, time for a break!

00:00:31.430 --> 00:00:37.170
<i>Ojo has been raiding during the team's
 defense practice game since last week.</i>

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:40.410
<i>The first-years have a good handle
 on how to develop themselves.</i>

00:00:41.930 --> 00:00:46.460
<i>However, Misumi, who has been paired 
on defense with Date all this time,</i>

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:52.170
<i>is unsure how to move as 
an anti in this new lineup.</i>

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:55.210
<i>What did I used to do...</i>

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:57.370
<i>before this guy was around?</i>

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:32.630
<b>April, one year earlier</b>

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:30.890
Thank you.

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:36.650
<i>A Battle 
\h\h\h\h\hof Wills</i>

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:37.150
You'll be living in a dorm, so you're 
going to have to look after yourself.

00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:39.890
And if you cause any trouble, 
you're not getting off easy.

00:02:39.890 --> 00:02:42.710
I get it already, Mom.

00:02:42.710 --> 00:02:45.140
But don't go hanging out 
with any snooty dweebs.

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:48.390
You sure have a lot of demands. 
Quit worrying about me!

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:57.140
Noukin High School

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:53.190
Middle school was the end 
of my wild days, okay?

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:54.540
I'll leave you to it, then.

00:02:57.150 --> 00:03:00.780
Sure thing. I'll spend my 
high school days happily.

00:03:05.050 --> 00:03:06.500
Then how about you give me your number...

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:08.480
You're Misumi Kyohei-kun, right?

00:03:09.890 --> 00:03:10.500
Huh?

00:03:11.650 --> 00:03:14.430
<i>My happy days ended quickly.</i>

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:18.670
<i>What?</i>

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:20.970
<i>I'll kill you!</i>

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:24.740
What truly splendid defensive moves!

00:03:24.740 --> 00:03:26.600
So splendid, I want to show 
them to all kinds of people!

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:29.640
Wh-What do you want here?

00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:36.760
Have you heard of kabaddi?

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:42.570
<i>Two senpai from the year above me, and...</i>

00:03:43.130 --> 00:03:46.070
<i>sometimes a few extra players from 
outside the club, that was the team.</i>

00:03:47.390 --> 00:03:49.200
<i>All right! I took him down!</i>

00:03:49.970 --> 00:03:51.960
<i>How was that? Good?</i>

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:56.630
<i>My brain stung from having to constantly 
strategize from second to second,</i>

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:59.660
<i>which suited my thrill-seeking 
personality very well.</i>

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:02.670
<i>In terms of power, I'm the best.</i>

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:05.340
Here he comes!

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:09.100
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:10.100
Kabaddi.

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:11.100
Strikers!

00:04:13.850 --> 00:04:14.710
Kabaddi.

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:15.800
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:21.710
<i>Even without him, 
I wasn't afraid of anything.</i>

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:26.360
Don't just attack directly. 
Use feints, too.

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:27.120
Sir!

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:34.860
We're losing fewer points, but we still 
haven't taken the captain down even once.

00:04:34.860 --> 00:04:36.880
Yeah, that's true.

00:04:37.260 --> 00:04:42.330
The way kabaddi is, if the defense is 
no good, there's no way to catch up.

00:04:44.270 --> 00:04:45.840
<i>In our first competition...</i>

00:04:46.330 --> 00:04:48.700
<i>we got matched up with a team of monsters.</i>

00:04:49.570 --> 00:04:52.520
<i>Our side was mostly players 
from outside the team,</i>

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:55.080
<i>and I was an absolute sitting duck.</i>

00:04:56.020 --> 00:04:58.400
<i>I was sent off the court over and over.</i>

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:07.450
<i>And every time, the captain managed 
to bring me back, scoring on raids.</i>

00:05:08.650 --> 00:05:11.690
<i>Over and over again...</i>

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:15.330
It was like I went back just 
to have points taken from me.

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:21.200
<i>I started thinking that it would 
be better if I wasn't there.</i>

00:05:25.040 --> 00:05:27.730
<i>After the tournament, the players who 
weren't part of the team disappeared.</i>

00:05:28.600 --> 00:05:30.720
<i>Scraping together a mishmash 
of players won't be enough.</i>

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:33.850
<i>We need a person with strong defensive
 capabilities who won't give up points.</i>

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:38.050
<i>I don't ever want to feel 
that miserable again!</i>

00:05:39.260 --> 00:05:40.300
<i>It's time to go scouting.</i>

00:05:42.490 --> 00:05:44.170
<i>I already knew who I wanted to target.</i>

00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:50.850
H-Hey, Date.

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:53.320
What is it you're always 
doing with that thing?

00:05:54.970 --> 00:05:56.870
Rehab for my tendons.

00:05:56.870 --> 00:05:59.070
They're already healed, 
but it's become a habit.

00:05:59.070 --> 00:06:01.410
<i>It's hard to make an opening 
gambit from "rehab."</i>

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:04.730
Are you in a club or on a team?

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:06.400
I was.

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:08.220
Baseball. I was a pitcher.

00:06:08.650 --> 00:06:11.320
But I can't move precisely 
enough anymore, so...

00:06:11.320 --> 00:06:12.640
<i>That's heavy!</i>

00:06:13.500 --> 00:06:15.610
I'm thinking about what I want to do.

00:06:15.610 --> 00:06:18.390
<i>This is the second term! 
That's too much thinking!</i>

00:06:18.890 --> 00:06:19.860
You know...

00:06:20.780 --> 00:06:23.550
if you haven't decided 
what you want to do yet...

00:06:25.600 --> 00:06:26.690
Come on!

00:06:27.390 --> 00:06:29.450
You'll be slow on the catch! Don't get scared!

00:06:30.030 --> 00:06:30.950
Yes, sir!

00:06:31.590 --> 00:06:34.910
<i>That guy... All he's got is the build, huh?</i>

00:06:34.910 --> 00:06:38.210
<i>And he's the clumsy type that 
can't put anything into practice.</i>

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:42.790
But don't go hanging out 
with any snooty dweebs.

00:06:44.140 --> 00:06:45.600
<i>You don't need to tell me.</i>

00:06:46.010 --> 00:06:48.720
<i>I'd be better off making moves on my own.</i>

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:56.720
<b>Winter Kabaddi Tournament
High School Division</b>

00:06:53.390 --> 00:06:56.320
<i>At our second competition...</i>

00:06:57.390 --> 00:06:59.930
<i>I made exactly the same mistakes.</i>

00:07:04.580 --> 00:07:06.920
<i>All that happened was we 
had more sitting ducks.</i>

00:07:07.990 --> 00:07:11.990
<b>Winter High School
Kabaddi Tournament
← Venue</b>

00:07:07.990 --> 00:07:11.990
<b>Gymnasium</b>

00:07:08.810 --> 00:07:10.440
Do you feel like quitting?

00:07:10.920 --> 00:07:11.990
A little.

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:13.380
Really?

00:07:13.380 --> 00:07:16.050
If you quit now, it'd be the 
same as baseball, wouldn't it?

00:07:16.780 --> 00:07:18.390
The reason I quit baseball was—

00:07:18.390 --> 00:07:19.750
Because you got injured, right?

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:23.780
But if you could have played a
 different position if you wanted.

00:07:24.450 --> 00:07:27.840
Don't say it like it's so easy! 
You are a flippant, foolish man!

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:30.170
Have you ever seriously 
devoted yourself to anything?!

00:07:31.500 --> 00:07:33.370
No, I haven't. What of it?

00:07:33.370 --> 00:07:35.330
That's why you can say it like it's nothing!

00:07:36.650 --> 00:07:38.490
Hey! Stop it, you two!

00:07:38.490 --> 00:07:39.520
Let go of me!

00:07:41.450 --> 00:07:43.190
Oh, there was something.

00:07:43.550 --> 00:07:46.150
Something I really threw myself into...

00:07:48.910 --> 00:07:50.300
Brawling!

00:07:51.020 --> 00:07:53.470
I figured you might be that kind of person!

00:07:53.470 --> 00:07:56.010
Our experiences are different, 
you snooty dweeb!

00:07:57.660 --> 00:07:59.200
<i>He's got so much power!</i>

00:08:02.300 --> 00:08:03.580
I'll beat you to death!

00:08:12.250 --> 00:08:15.030
A fighting spirit is important in kabaddi,

00:08:15.030 --> 00:08:16.970
but punching is against the rules.

00:08:17.390 --> 00:08:19.960
We're all sharing in this frustration,

00:08:20.380 --> 00:08:20.940
aren't we?

00:08:26.140 --> 00:08:28.570
<i>This isn't something I can tell the new guys.</i>

00:08:29.390 --> 00:08:30.950
Misumi-senpai?

00:08:30.950 --> 00:08:32.980
What's wrong? You stopped talking.

00:08:32.980 --> 00:08:35.690
Huh? Oh.

00:08:35.690 --> 00:08:38.880
Should we try to come up with some kind 
of strategy to take down the captain?

00:08:38.880 --> 00:08:39.770
Sir!

00:08:47.180 --> 00:08:48.670
Hey, Misumi.

00:08:50.010 --> 00:08:52.810
Huh? You out running, too?

00:08:52.810 --> 00:08:53.800
Yeah.

00:08:54.040 --> 00:08:55.240
Hey, Shin...

00:08:55.800 --> 00:08:58.540
The captain's arms are really 
scrawny, aren't they?

00:08:58.540 --> 00:09:00.430
What is this all of a sudden?

00:09:00.430 --> 00:09:03.300
You remember that time we stopped 
fighting before we realized it?

00:09:03.300 --> 00:09:04.830
Ah, you mean that time, huh?

00:09:05.290 --> 00:09:07.460
It's embarrassing, so I don't 
really want to remember.

00:09:09.100 --> 00:09:12.940
But you know, after that, we started 
being able to work together for real.

00:09:13.480 --> 00:09:15.860
While we were out goofing around,

00:09:15.860 --> 00:09:18.700
we ended up becoming buddies 
without even realizing it.

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:21.350
Let's forget that for a while.

00:09:21.830 --> 00:09:24.080
I'll end up connecting with 
you again eventually, Shin.

00:09:25.060 --> 00:09:30.030
Right now, growing and assisting the captain
 is the coolest thing we can do, right?

00:09:30.920 --> 00:09:31.920
That's true.

00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:36.080
So, who will be the first 
to take down the captain?

00:09:36.080 --> 00:09:37.290
Are we competing?

00:09:37.290 --> 00:09:39.940
Huh? No.

00:09:40.410 --> 00:09:42.930
I'm saying we should go back 
to how we were way back then.

00:09:43.340 --> 00:09:44.240
Huh?

00:09:44.240 --> 00:09:45.930
What I'm saying is...

00:09:46.710 --> 00:09:48.060
this is a brawl.

00:09:50.070 --> 00:09:51.110
I see.

00:09:59.500 --> 00:10:01.580
Hey, Hitomi. Come here a sec.

00:10:02.220 --> 00:10:05.040
They seem to have changed quite 
a bit over the last few days.

00:10:05.590 --> 00:10:07.670
They do.

00:10:07.670 --> 00:10:11.480
Yoigoshi seems to be consciously making 
plays that help those around him shine.

00:10:12.090 --> 00:10:13.440
And that cautious Date

00:10:13.440 --> 00:10:16.850
has started moving decisively, 
without worrying about how he looks.

00:10:18.600 --> 00:10:20.360
It's not just those two, either.

00:10:20.360 --> 00:10:22.100
Captain!

00:10:22.870 --> 00:10:24.120
If you would!

00:10:25.090 --> 00:10:25.700
Sure!

00:10:25.700 --> 00:10:28.600
Team Kyohei, I'm coming to raid.

00:10:30.240 --> 00:10:32.130
Thank you for your help!

00:10:37.320 --> 00:10:40.860
Kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:10:41.090 --> 00:10:44.760
<i>Both Azemichi and Misumi have 
always had a high skill level,</i>

00:10:44.760 --> 00:10:46.500
<i>but there's something that's 
overwhelmingly lacking.</i>

00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:48.870
<i>That is...</i>

00:10:50.780 --> 00:10:52.880
<i>the ability to strategize.</i>

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:53.880
<i>He's coming!</i>

00:10:56.820 --> 00:10:58.990
<i>"I'm coming in for a tackle now."</i>

00:10:59.410 --> 00:11:01.900
<i>They unconsciously send 
the enemy those signals.</i>

00:11:02.390 --> 00:11:05.040
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:11:03.060 --> 00:11:05.040
<i>Through continuous threats,</i>

00:11:05.040 --> 00:11:07.580
<i>they could divert attention 
from their real catch attempt.</i>

00:11:08.890 --> 00:11:11.900
Kabaddi... Kabaddi!

00:11:09.490 --> 00:11:10.310
<i>But...</i>

00:11:14.900 --> 00:11:16.090
Kabaddi!

00:11:15.470 --> 00:11:17.140
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:11:18.730 --> 00:11:21.720
<i>Experience allows one to see 
through a moment's inattention.</i>

00:11:22.400 --> 00:11:24.910
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:11:22.640 --> 00:11:23.910
Blast it!

00:11:28.180 --> 00:11:30.700
Okay, next, Shinji's team!

00:11:30.700 --> 00:11:31.420
Sir!

00:11:32.420 --> 00:11:34.690
<i>This team has a long history in sports.</i>

00:11:35.900 --> 00:11:38.160
<i>They can make plans and 
move together, but...</i>

00:11:38.160 --> 00:11:40.920
Kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:11:41.720 --> 00:11:43.910
You're letting him rest! 
Go put some pressure on him!

00:11:44.380 --> 00:11:47.940
<i>They understand how to set up traps for 
their opponents, but, conversely...</i>

00:11:47.940 --> 00:11:48.680
Is he retreating?

00:11:50.240 --> 00:11:51.180
Kabaddi.

00:11:51.650 --> 00:11:53.800
<i>They're not good at 
confronting the unexpected.</i>

00:11:54.450 --> 00:11:55.480
Kabaddi.

00:11:54.800 --> 00:11:56.370
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:11:55.530 --> 00:11:57.190
<i>Staying calm and rational isn't enough.</i>

00:11:58.090 --> 00:12:00.190
<i>Being bold and dauntless isn't enough, either.</i>

00:12:01.400 --> 00:12:05.230
<i>A combination of wildness and 
rationality is the ideal in kabaddi.</i>

00:12:06.370 --> 00:12:08.140
<i>Everyone has their own disposition.</i>

00:12:08.140 --> 00:12:10.200
<i>It isn't something that can 
be achieved with words alone.</i>

00:12:12.210 --> 00:12:13.400
I'm not letting you get back!

00:12:13.850 --> 00:12:16.210
<i>The one closest to the ideal is Yoigoshi.</i>

00:12:16.890 --> 00:12:18.210
<i>The perfect ideal is...</i>

00:12:18.980 --> 00:12:20.120
<i>Masato...</i>

00:12:23.600 --> 00:12:28.220
<i>I'm not sure we have any members
 who can reach Masato's level.</i>

00:12:28.990 --> 00:12:31.090
Hitomi, step out for a minute.

00:12:31.090 --> 00:12:32.660
Oh. Yes, sir.

00:12:35.380 --> 00:12:36.330
Okay.

00:12:37.820 --> 00:12:39.060
Team Kyohei...

00:12:39.600 --> 00:12:42.090
He's taking breaks in between, but...

00:12:42.090 --> 00:12:44.490
...the captain doesn't look tired at all.

00:12:45.310 --> 00:12:47.280
What do you think, Azemichi?

00:12:47.280 --> 00:12:49.640
It's working. That face.

00:12:49.640 --> 00:12:51.750
We've been using it to 
intimidate him this whole time.

00:12:52.690 --> 00:12:53.800
I'm exhausted.

00:12:54.750 --> 00:12:57.840
I guess I really just don't get it.

00:12:58.330 --> 00:13:00.300
It doesn't show on his face.

00:13:00.970 --> 00:13:02.050
<i>Since forever ago,</i>

00:13:02.730 --> 00:13:06.260
<i>you've charged toward the enemy 
with a nonchalant expression</i>

00:13:06.720 --> 00:13:08.440
<i>and saved us countless times.</i>

00:13:09.140 --> 00:13:14.130
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:13:12.140 --> 00:13:14.590
<i>There's no way it was so easy, right?</i>

00:13:15.130 --> 00:13:18.150
<i>You were desperate because our 
defense was so weak, right?</i>

00:13:18.600 --> 00:13:20.150
<i>Another threat?</i>

00:13:20.380 --> 00:13:22.150
<i>His center of gravity is forward.</i>

00:13:22.440 --> 00:13:23.750
<i>He's really coming in for a catch—</i>

00:13:26.430 --> 00:13:27.660
<i>Kyohei was a decoy!</i>

00:13:27.660 --> 00:13:32.660
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:13:33.450 --> 00:13:35.860
<i>He came in at the same time
 as Soma and Ban-kun.</i>

00:13:37.070 --> 00:13:40.020
<i>If Kyohei wasn't meant to be a decoy, then...</i>

00:13:40.020 --> 00:13:42.410
<i>they used him as a decoy at the last minute.</i>

00:13:43.550 --> 00:13:45.240
<i>Did they do it on instinct?</i>

00:13:46.480 --> 00:13:49.170
Sorry. I knew it was coming, but...

00:13:49.170 --> 00:13:52.430
That was more than enough. 
You managed to surprise him. That's amazing!

00:13:52.980 --> 00:13:54.860
<i>Now we just have to do what we planned.</i>

00:13:55.430 --> 00:13:59.810
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:13:59.810 --> 00:14:00.730
He's coming!

00:14:01.250 --> 00:14:02.070
Kabaddi.

00:14:11.400 --> 00:14:13.770
<i>It seems Soma really can read my movements.</i>

00:14:14.460 --> 00:14:16.840
<i>That's good teamwork. 
I've got nowhere to run.</i>

00:14:19.280 --> 00:14:22.170
<i>First, I'll use a counter 
to put Kyohei behind me.</i>

00:14:24.720 --> 00:14:25.710
<i>He stopped?!</i>

00:14:26.150 --> 00:14:26.970
Kabaddi...

00:14:27.550 --> 00:14:29.970
Take the lead and grab his leg,

00:14:29.970 --> 00:14:31.950
right, Misumi-senpai?

00:14:34.220 --> 00:14:35.400
<i>Those guys...</i>

00:14:36.110 --> 00:14:37.150
<i>are strategizing?</i>

00:14:40.930 --> 00:14:42.480
<i>He used a counter!</i>

00:14:44.260 --> 00:14:47.300
<i>Maybe... if I weren't here...</i>

00:14:48.450 --> 00:14:50.440
<i>everything would be better...</i>

00:14:56.230 --> 00:14:58.770
<i>I'm sorry for putting up 
such a pathetic defense!</i>

00:14:59.230 --> 00:15:00.380
<i>From now on...</i>

00:15:01.730 --> 00:15:03.590
<i>I'll be able to take you down...</i>

00:15:03.590 --> 00:15:04.840
<i>with this strength!</i>

00:15:10.520 --> 00:15:12.300
<i>I will repay my debt to you.</i>

00:15:14.090 --> 00:15:16.160
<i>The opponent's territory! It's so close!</i>

00:15:15.980 --> 00:15:16.660
Kabaddi.

00:15:16.360 --> 00:15:17.630
<i>I won't let you reach it!</i>

00:15:17.630 --> 00:15:18.430
Kabaddi.

00:15:18.430 --> 00:15:19.940
<i>If I let him make it back,</i>

00:15:19.940 --> 00:15:24.270
<i>then I'll still be my pathetic self 
who's always saved by the captain!</i>

00:15:24.270 --> 00:15:27.430
<i>I will become a strength for the captain!</i>

00:15:27.430 --> 00:15:29.020
<i>A strong man!</i>

00:15:29.740 --> 00:15:32.460
<i>A cool man! That's what I will become!</i>

00:15:32.950 --> 00:15:34.200
Kabaddi.

00:15:39.470 --> 00:15:40.770
He made it back.

00:15:43.180 --> 00:15:44.250
Kyohei.

00:15:44.730 --> 00:15:45.520
Yeah?

00:15:49.510 --> 00:15:54.970
I didn't think you'd force me
 into a battle of wills.

00:15:57.250 --> 00:16:00.680
<i>It wasn't just skills 
I lack in... but will, too?</i>

00:16:01.820 --> 00:16:04.270
Damn it! I am so uncool!

00:16:04.270 --> 00:16:05.590
Uncool?

00:16:06.730 --> 00:16:07.820
He's on the ground.

00:16:08.510 --> 00:16:11.690
That's a man that neither of us 
could do anything against before.

00:16:13.870 --> 00:16:16.160
You pushed him all the way 
into a battle of wills.

00:16:17.160 --> 00:16:21.070
Isn't that what you'd call cool?

00:16:23.100 --> 00:16:24.580
No one asked you.

00:16:24.970 --> 00:16:26.940
Quit saying stuff like that.

00:16:30.340 --> 00:16:32.680
I told you, this is a brawl.

00:16:33.100 --> 00:16:34.600
I'm not cut out for such a thing.

00:16:37.650 --> 00:16:40.310
Let's stop doing this kind of practice.

00:16:40.310 --> 00:16:40.890
What?

00:16:41.640 --> 00:16:44.170
There's no weight to my raids.

00:16:44.170 --> 00:16:48.450
If you get too used to me, you'll have 
a hard time with other types of raiders.

00:16:48.450 --> 00:16:49.800
Time for the next step.

00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:53.750
When you're in a group, 
your individual quirks stand out.

00:16:54.730 --> 00:16:58.970
Based on the quirks I've seen, 
I'll give each of you a technique.

00:17:02.190 --> 00:17:04.250
<i>Techniques, huh?</i>

00:17:05.500 --> 00:17:07.760
You want something more stimulating?

00:17:07.760 --> 00:17:09.650
Something overwhelmingly electrifying.

00:17:09.650 --> 00:17:11.000
A practice match.

00:17:11.000 --> 00:17:12.320
But...

00:17:12.320 --> 00:17:15.160
We already played Souwa earlier, so...

00:17:15.160 --> 00:17:17.930
there isn't anywhere else that would play us.

00:17:18.240 --> 00:17:19.670
There's somewhere we could try.

00:17:19.670 --> 00:17:20.430
You're kidding!

00:17:20.910 --> 00:17:23.540
I'm sure you must be wanting 
to see them by now.

00:17:24.400 --> 00:17:26.380
Oh! Do you mean...

00:17:28.540 --> 00:17:30.930
Thanks for everything you've done for us.

00:17:30.930 --> 00:17:33.420
Sakura-kun! We'll be waiting 
for you in high school!

00:17:34.920 --> 00:17:35.610
Yes, sir.

00:17:36.340 --> 00:17:40.570
I will become a raider that can 
be a strength for you, Ojo-san,

00:17:40.570 --> 00:17:41.690
then I will come see you.

00:17:43.130 --> 00:17:46.460
Our plans have changed 
quite a bit from back then.

