00:17:59.090 --> 00:18:02.100
<b>Akagakubo Station</b>

00:18:02.430 --> 00:18:04.380
We're here!

00:18:04.380 --> 00:18:06.790
Are there strong players 
in a place like this?

00:18:06.790 --> 00:18:09.730
Yeah. At a place called 
Saitama Kouyou High School.

00:18:10.250 --> 00:18:11.430
Never heard of it.

00:18:11.430 --> 00:18:13.520
Saitama Kouyou?!

00:18:13.520 --> 00:18:17.160
They were quarterfinalists in the
 Kanto Winter Tournament last year!

00:18:17.160 --> 00:18:19.430
Souwa placed fourth, 
making them better, right?

00:18:19.430 --> 00:18:21.240
In terms of placing, yes, but...

00:18:22.180 --> 00:18:25.900
They started their team last year, 
and their oldest members are second-years.

00:18:26.490 --> 00:18:30.500
When they made the quarterfinals 
last year, they were all first-years.

00:18:31.500 --> 00:18:34.640
And two of them are our juniors 
from the national selections.

00:18:35.150 --> 00:18:37.010
We used those connections again for today.

00:18:37.520 --> 00:18:40.020
No wonder they're so strong.

00:18:40.020 --> 00:18:40.810
Here they are.

00:18:45.770 --> 00:18:48.590
Welcome to everyone from Noukin High School!

00:18:49.020 --> 00:18:54.020
<b>Saitama Kouyou High School Second-Year
Sakura Manabu</b>

00:18:49.020 --> 00:18:54.020
<b>Saitama Kouyou High School Second-Year, Captain
Uto Hiromoto</b>

00:18:49.930 --> 00:18:51.800
We're from Saitama Kouyou!

00:18:51.800 --> 00:18:53.340
We're pleased to have you!

00:18:54.490 --> 00:18:58.810
We're from Noukin High School. 
Thank you for having us!

00:18:58.810 --> 00:18:59.880
Thank you!

00:19:02.030 --> 00:19:03.240
Hey, Hiro...

00:19:03.690 --> 00:19:06.070
D-Did you hear that, Sakura?

00:19:06.070 --> 00:19:09.540
Masato-san and Kei-san used 
polite language with us!

00:19:11.200 --> 00:19:13.290
We're from different schools! 
What else did you expect?

00:19:13.790 --> 00:19:14.730
Ojo-san.

00:19:18.800 --> 00:19:24.300
Health and Long Life

00:19:19.850 --> 00:19:23.130
I made a promised to become a 
raider who would be a strength for you,

00:19:23.130 --> 00:19:24.300
but I couldn't keep it...

00:19:24.900 --> 00:19:26.420
I'm very sorry.

00:19:26.420 --> 00:19:30.810
I feel like I only ever see you bowing to me.

00:19:32.050 --> 00:19:33.260
Don't worry about it.

00:19:33.260 --> 00:19:35.160
You had to deal with a lot concerning 
your grandma, too, right?

00:19:35.160 --> 00:19:37.320
I'm just glad you came back.

00:19:39.370 --> 00:19:42.070
And I've been raising up some other raiders.

00:19:42.420 --> 00:19:43.770
Him, you mean?

00:19:49.790 --> 00:19:53.330
I know it's strange for me to say this 
when I'm from another school, but...

00:19:54.270 --> 00:19:57.840
please work hard so that you 
will be a strength for Ojo-san.

00:19:58.570 --> 00:20:00.290
I'll leave it to you.

00:20:00.290 --> 00:20:02.950
Huh? Uh, sure.

00:20:04.560 --> 00:20:07.580
Sakura is a raider, just like you are.

00:20:07.580 --> 00:20:09.360
He'll be an interesting opponent.

00:20:09.360 --> 00:20:10.970
An interesting opponent?

00:20:11.350 --> 00:20:14.680
Iura-senpai's strategy makes sense.

00:20:14.680 --> 00:20:17.930
By omitting any detailed 
explanations for us rookies,

00:20:17.930 --> 00:20:20.370
he applies a moderate sense 
of anxiety and tension.

00:20:20.370 --> 00:20:22.570
He is a person who has done that endlessly...

00:20:23.360 --> 00:20:27.870
For Yoigoshi-san, going up against another 
raider will create a sense of tension...

00:20:24.250 --> 00:20:26.560
We should brace ourselves. too.

00:20:26.560 --> 00:20:27.200
Yeah.

00:20:34.580 --> 00:20:35.610
We finally...

00:20:36.090 --> 00:20:37.440
...made it!

00:20:36.400 --> 00:20:40.380
Ojo

00:20:37.440 --> 00:20:40.380
Whoa! It sure is huge.

00:20:40.810 --> 00:20:42.710
Why is it so deep in the mountains?

00:20:43.180 --> 00:20:47.110
This place is used for elementary and
 middle school field trips and nature camps.

00:20:47.110 --> 00:20:48.470
It's a nature park.

00:20:48.890 --> 00:20:51.580
And there's a gym. We use it all the time.

00:20:52.780 --> 00:20:55.130
If we're going to have our 
practice match in the afternoon,

00:20:55.130 --> 00:20:58.050
then we can have a 
group practice first, right?

00:20:58.050 --> 00:20:58.770
Yeah.

00:21:01.730 --> 00:21:18.250
<b>Keep the
Locker Rooms
Clean!!</b>

00:21:02.160 --> 00:21:05.440
I wonder what kind of training those guys do.

00:21:05.440 --> 00:21:06.620
Who knows?

00:21:06.620 --> 00:21:11.000
You saw them climb the mountain paths like 
it was nothing, like Azemichi, right?

00:21:11.000 --> 00:21:14.010
If they can gain that kind of stamina, 
they'll do pretty well.

00:21:14.460 --> 00:21:17.720
Does that mean everyone 
around here's like Azemichi?

00:21:19.050 --> 00:21:22.300
Is that what you meant earlier when you 
said he'd be an interesting opponent?

00:21:22.300 --> 00:21:23.760
Well, there is that, but...

00:21:24.500 --> 00:21:29.490
Sakura really admired one particular raider 
and learned most of his skills from him.

00:21:30.860 --> 00:21:34.170
Just like you, he learned from Ojo Masato.

00:21:38.260 --> 00:21:40.460
You guys are sort of like fellow apprentices.

00:21:40.920 --> 00:21:42.540
It'll make for a good match, right?

00:21:44.700 --> 00:21:47.900
He suddenly sounds like a much 
more troublesome player to me.

00:21:53.080 --> 00:21:55.570
We'll start with defense training.

00:21:55.570 --> 00:21:58.540
Is there anyone willing to be the raider?

00:21:59.470 --> 00:22:00.570
I'd like to.

00:22:13.760 --> 00:22:15.150
Kabaddi...

00:23:49.030 --> 00:23:54.250
<b>Next Time
"Because He's the Ace"</b>

00:23:49.440 --> 00:23:52.530
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:23:50.110 --> 00:23:52.530
Next time, "Because He's the Ace!"

00:23:52.530 --> 00:23:53.320
Kabaddi!
